# Written into the workspace by google-github-actions/auth@v2 — the action's
# own README says to ignore it. It is an external_account (Workload Identity
# Federation) CONFIG file, not a key: it carries the audience, token URL and
# service-account impersonation URL, and no private_key. The OIDC token it
# exchanges lives only in the runner, so the file authenticates nothing once it
# leaves CI.
#
# It still must not be committed. On 2026-09-23 the changesets release job
# picked it up alongside the version bump and put it in the "version packages"
# PR, where GitGuardian flagged it — disclosing the WIF pool and the
# impersonated service account, which is reconnaissance rather than access, and
# blocking a release either way.
gha-creds-*.json
